# CRYPTOBOT environment template.
# Copy to `.env` locally and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`
# (it is gitignored; `git check-ignore -v .env` proves it).
# Never paste these values into chat, tickets, logs, or a report.
#
# Nothing here is loaded automatically. The application has no dotenv
# dependency and never reads a file: it reads only the two variable *names*
# named in `config/trading.yaml` (`alpaca.api_key_env`, `alpaca.api_secret_env`)
# from the process environment. Export the values in the same shell that will
# run the bot. `cryptobot env-hint --shell powershell|bash` prints the exact
# syntax and whether each name is currently set - it never reads a value.
#
# No credentials are needed for simulated mode, backtests, research, the test
# suite, or any read-only command. They are required for `cryptobot data-refresh`
# and `cryptobot paper-run`. Without them `preflight` fails by design rather
# than quietly running something that only looks like paper trading.

# --- Alpaca PAPER account keys (required only for `paper-run`) --------------
# Generate at: https://app.alpaca.markets/paper/dashboard/overview
# Paper keys only. Live keys are neither required nor supported: the trading
# base URL is checked against the paper allowlist and `cryptobot config-check`
# refuses an `app.environment` other than `paper`.
ALPACA_API_KEY=replace_me_paper_key_id
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=replace_me_paper_secret_key

# If you rename either variable, change `alpaca.api_key_env` /
# `alpaca.api_secret_env` in `config/trading.yaml` to match. The configuration
# holds names, never values, so it stays safe to commit and to print.

# --- Telegram notifications (optional) --------------------------------------
# Both are required for notifications to work; `monitoring.telegram_enabled`
# in `config/trading.yaml` is the switch. Tokens are redacted from log output.
CRYPTOBOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=replace_me
CRYPTOBOT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=replace_me

# --- Optional journal location override -------------------------------------
# Overrides `journal.path` from the configuration. A relative path resolves
# against the project root. Useful for keeping a soak run's database separate.
# CRYPTOBOT_DB=var/cryptobot.db
